{
  "season": 1,
  "week": 15,
  "articles": [
    {
      "id": "injury-report-s1-w15",
      "type": "feature",
      "author": "ellis-quill",
      "title": "Injury Report: Thorpe and Mr. Clanky face long absences",
      "dek": "Mt. Silver and Lavender prepare new passing plans; Mahogany loses Watchog; the full league recovery comparison.",
      "teams": [
        "goldenrod",
        "ecruteak",
        "mahogany",
        "mossdeep",
        "sunyshore"
      ],
      "frontPageOrder": 0.4,
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Two winning teams lose important passers"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mt. Silver’s Tic Thorpe has a new six-week report after throwing for 244 yards and two touchdowns against Saffron. Josh Alakazam still has seven reported weeks remaining. Crem Ftzpatrik completed five of eight for 69 yards and a touchdown, then directed the winning field-goal drive. His actual relief work makes him a demonstrated option before Cinnabar; a future starting assignment still requires the team’s decision. Foo Warner has a new two-week report, and cornerback Ninjask has one."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Lavender’s Mr. Clanky has a new eight-week report. His listed position is SLOT, but he completed six of eight passes for 121 yards and a touchdown against Celadon. Frosmoth supplied 163 passing yards in the same win. The Wails must prepare the available passing group for Cerulean while People Eater remains out two weeks. The injury record does not identify either passer’s precise injury play."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "New absences around the league"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mahogany’s outside linebacker Watchog has a new seventeen-week report, the largest new recovery duration this week. Jellicent is out two weeks, adding another receiving absence while Golduck continues his recovery. The Frost visit Vermilion, whose offense was shut out at Olivine. Their defensive replacements must preserve the opportunity created by that matchup."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Cinnabar’s Seismitoad has a new two-week report after four carries for 16 yards. Pidgeotto finished the Blackthorn win with useful late runs and totaled 25 yards on three attempts; he is one observed contributor for the staff to consider before Mt. Silver. Oreburgh’s fullback Swampert is newly out four weeks before Dewford. Cianwood receiver Doduo has one week, and Azalea safety Castform has two. These are reported durations rather than guaranteed return dates."
        },
        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Recovery changes before the marquee matchup"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mossdeep’s Marshall Flock and Luvrelle Revis have cleared their previous positive recovery counters. Sunyshore’s FLOAT SZN has also cleared his. Those changes improve the availability picture before the Starseekers visit the Eclipse, but do not establish an appearance or starting role. Serp Gardener still has one reported week, Ninjaskamara one and Richard Furman two. Rustboro’s My Way, Son has three before Canalave."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The full table compares the current report with the previous issue, separating new injuries from ordinary countdown changes and cleared designations. Zero weeks means no remaining absence is reported; it does not establish game participation. Positions are the current listed positions. No diagnoses, unsupported doubtful labels or certain return dates are added."
        },
